INSTALL for Midi66 v. 0.2.0 and above
Chris Ahlstrom
2026-10-17 to 2026-11-17

The Midi66 library is intended to replace the "midi" directories of
the rtl66 project, for better encapsulation and re-use. It contains
only the code needed to process MIDI data and MIDI files.

Meson is the build system for the Midi66 library. Meson 1.4 and above is
required. The 'meson.options' file replaces 'meson_options.txt'.

In order to simplify life, a POSIX shell script, 'work.sh', is provided.
The most important options are:

    -   --clean. Removes *all* build products and test results from the
        build directory.
    -   --debug. Build the library and test code in DEBUG mode.
    -   --clang. Build the code using the Clang compiler.
    -   --help. Show all available options; there are many  more than
        these.

Build:

    $ ./work.sh --clean (when Meson build/options files change)
    $ ./work.sh --clang (if desired, to use Clang)
    $ ./work.sh         (use default compiler)

Tests:

    TO DO $ ./tests/tests.sh
    TO DO This script runs all of the tests listed in the file
    TO DO './library/tests/testlines.list', plus a couple more.

Install:

    The easiest way to install is to use the 'work.sh' script after rebuilding
    for release (i.e. no debug code):

    $ ./work.sh --clean
    $ ./work.sh --release
    $ ./work.sh --install

    Of course, one can use Meson without this script if desired. Study the
    script for details.

Subproject:

    If one does not want to install Midi66, Meson '*.wrap' files are
    provided to use Midi66 as a Meson subproject.

    -   Make sure the using project is built using Meson.
    -   Create a 'subprojects' directory in the using project.
    -   Copy the desired '.wrap' file from the 'extras/wraps' directory
        into 'subprojects'.
    -   Build!

Build tools:

    -   C/C++ compiler. On Linux etc., the GNU and Clang compilers are
        supported. On Windows, currently tested only with the Mingw compiler.
    -   Python.
    -   Meson and Ninja. In Windows, they can be installed from
        the same Meson release '*.msi' file.
    -   C++17 and above is required to build Midi66. The GNU and Clang
        compilers support it.

# vim: sw=4 ts=4 wm=4 et ft=sh
